ith this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "fieldsOfStudy": ["Computer Science"], "publicationDate": null, "authors": [{"authorId": "2242949023", "name": "C. Cui"}, {"authorId": "2109267955", "name": "Yunsheng Ma"}, {"authorId": "2267506629", "name": "Zi-Chong Yang"}, {"authorId": "2275030995", "name": "Yu-Peng Zhou"}, {"authorId": "2271451076", "name": "Peiran Liu"}, {"authorId": "2053819036", "name": "Juan-Wu Lu"}, {"authorId": "2282544504", "name": "Ling-Xi Li"}, {"authorId": "2327177899", "name": "Yao-Bin Chen"}, {"authorId": "1757039", "name": "J. Panchal"}, {"authorId": "48846470", "name": "Amr Abdelraouf"}, {"authorId": "2261696435", "name": "Rohit Gupta"}, {"authorId": "2261909117", "name": "Kyungtae Han"}, {"authorId": "4141749", "name": "Zi-Ran Wang"}], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "82cbf4ce6db5c5d7ec6ffdbcfd3147e6c8f33df5", "externalIds": {"DBLP": "conf/nips/ChenW0JFYW24", "DOI": "10.52202/079017-0600", "CorpusId": 276185269}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/82cbf4ce6db5c5d7ec6ffdbcfd3147e6c8f33df5", "title": "Policy Learning from Tutorial Books via Understanding, Rehearsing and Introspecting", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "https://discovery.ucl.ac.uk/10207118/1/7398_Policy_Learning_from_Tuto.pdf", "status": "GREEN", "license": "other-oa", "disclaimer": "Notice: Paper or abstract available at https://api.unpaywall.org/v2/10.52202/079017-0600?email=<INSERT_YOUR_EMAIL> or https://doi.org/10.52202/079017-0600, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "fieldsOfStudy": ["Computer Science"], "publicationDate": null, "authors": [{"authorId": "2108968873", "name": "Xiong-Hui Chen"}, {"authorId": "2142663126", "name": "Ziyan Wang"}, {"authorId": "2269828122", "name": "Ya-Li Du"}, {"authorId": "2119326931", "name": "Shengyi Jiang"}, {"authorId": "2257271855", "name": "Meng Fang"}, {"authorId": "2344591380", "name": "Yang Yu"}, {"authorId": "2257572528", "name": "Jun Wang"}], "abstract": "When humans need to learn a new skill, we can acquire knowledge through written books, including textbooks, tutorials, etc. However, current research for decision-making, like reinforcement learning (RL), has primarily required numerous real interactions with the target environment to learn a skill, while failing to utilize the existing knowledge already summarized in the text. The success of Large Language Models (LLMs) sheds light on utilizing such knowledge behind the books. In this paper, we discuss a new policy learning problem called P olicy L earning from tutorial B ooks (PLfB) upon the shoulders of LLMs\u2019 systems, which aims to leverage rich resources such as tutorial books to derive a policy network. Inspired by how humans learn from books, we solve the problem via a three-stage framework: U nderstanding, R ehearsing, and I ntrospecting (URI). In particular, it first rehearses decision-making trajectories based on the derived knowledge after understanding the books, then introspects about the imaginary dataset to distill a policy network. We build two benchmarks for PLfB based on Tic-Tac-Toe and Football games. In the experiment, URI\u2019s policy achieves a minimum of 44% net winning rate against GPT-based agents without any real data. In the much more complex football game, URI\u2019s policy beat the built-in AIs with a 37% winning rate while GPT-based agents can only achieve a 6% winning rate. The project page"}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "be940a313721eff13183e7c3c17ea2a6ad93f567", "externalIds": {"DBLP": "journals/corr/abs-2403-16689", "DOI": "10.48550/arXiv.2403.16689", "CorpusId": 279031508}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/be940a313721eff13183e7c3c17ea2a6ad93f567", "title": "Synapse: Learning Preferential Concepts from Visual Demonstrations", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: The following paper fields have been elided by the publisher: {'abstract'}. Paper or abstract available at https://api.unpaywall.org/v2/10.48550/arXiv.2403.16689?email=<INSERT_YOUR_EMAIL> or https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2403.16689, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "fieldsOfStudy": ["Computer Science"], "publicationDate": null, "authors": [{"authorId": "2274501520", "name": "Sadanand Modak"}, {"authorId": "1577978380", "name": "Noah T Patton"}, {"authorId": "1714075", "name": "I. Dillig"}, {"authorId": "2267334183", "name": "Joydeep Biswas"}], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "a25e131813cb42e0809faed6204b8d39bf290978", "externalIds": {"DBLP": "journals/corr/abs-2404-07774", "DOI": "10.48550/arXiv.2404.07774", "CorpusId": 269042745}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/a25e131813cb42e0809faed6204b8d39bf290978", "title": "Sketch-Plan-Generalize: Continual Few-Shot Learning of Inductively Generalizable Spatial Concepts for Language-Guided Robot Manipulation", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: The following paper fields have been elided by the publisher: {'abstract'}. Paper or abstract available at https://api.unpaywall.org/v2/10.48550/arXiv.2404.07774?email=<INSERT_YOUR_EMAIL> or https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2404.07774, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "fieldsOfStudy": ["Computer Science"], "publicationDate": null, "authors": [{"authorId": "2149085911", "name": "Namasivayam Kalithasan"}, {"authorId": "2295988496", "name": "Sachit Sachdeva"}, {"authorId": "2190751709", "name": "H. Singh"}, {"authorId": "27543974", "name": "Divyanshu Aggarwal"}, {"aut